the Mink Warriors so easily.

261
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:02,205
Whoever those men are,
they're terribly strong.

262
00:20:02,420 --> 00:20:03,250
CP0.

263
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:04,848
They're a Cipher pole unit.

264
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,400
We saw them before, back in Dressrosa.

265
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:09,557
They're government officers, right?

266
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,577
Intelligence agents?

267
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:12,460
But what are they doing here?

268
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,777
And why are they looking
for you at a time like this?

269
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:19,300
I couldn't say, but we're
facing the worst-case scenario.

270
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:21,920
That much is apparent, at least. What?

271
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:26,520
CP0 is the top-ranked
unit in all of Cypherpole.

272
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:30,845
And the masked agents are the
most dangerous, even amongst them.

273
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:36,194
It seems that our escape
options are a little bare-bond.

274
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:37,460
Yo-ho-ho!

275
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:38,590
Well, look at you!

276
00:20:38,673 --> 00:20:41,860
No, no, come on, let's
get you to somewhere safe.

277
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:43,560
Time to fly!

278
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:52,760
Where are you? Choo-ji!

279
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:56,120
This is a disaster.

280
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:57,730
Choo-ji!

281
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:06,300
Um, excuse me?

282
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:08,099
Could you help me?

283
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:09,600
Whoever you are.

284
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:12,420
Judge used to talk about this.

285
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:14,317
Please, I have nothing to do with this.

286
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:16,257
I'm just a geisha from the Capitol.

287
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:20,060
He wanted to create the
perfect soldier. Shut up.

288
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:22,980
With incredible strength
and a heart of ice.

289
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:26,320
Powerful and merciless. Shut up.

290
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,793
I just want to go home.

291
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:29,137
Can you help me get out of here?

292
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:33,808
Don't pretend you're not excited to show
off that germ of blood in your veins.

293
00:21:33,900 --> 00:21:35,488
I'm not like them, damn it.

294
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:37,860
I'm human!

295
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:54,960
Are you okay, miss? Stay back!

296
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:58,160
Don't come any closer!

297
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:11,020
I need help!

298
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:15,140
Osume, what happened?

299
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:16,661
You're bleeding!

300
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:18,196
Who did this to you?

301
00:22:19,540 --> 00:22:22,240
Miss, are you alright? Let me help you.

302
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:26,200
How dare you attack this poor girl!

303
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:27,880
You call yourself a man!

304
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:30,197
Please, you've got this wrong.

305
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:32,240
I would never... Excuses!

306
00:22:32,420 --> 00:22:34,717
You're fighting on the
side of Wano, aren't you?

307
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:35,840
Of course I am.

308
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:38,537
Then you're doing this to your own people.

309
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:39,740
Listen to me.

310
00:22:39,940 --> 00:22:41,877
I don't know what happened to her.

311
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:44,120
I just showed up and...

312
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:46,337
I didn't...

313
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:47,700
I didn't do anything.

314
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:52,760
I didn't lay a finger on her.

315
00:22:52,940 --> 00:22:54,337
I was just...

316
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:55,500
I don't know.

317
00:22:57,740 --> 00:22:59,937
If you're so innocent, why did she run?

318
00:23:00,020 --> 00:23:01,457
I don't want to hear a word.

319
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:02,857
It doesn't matter what you say.

320
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:04,077
We're trying to hide.

321
00:23:04,160 --> 00:23:06,157
Now leave before someone finds this place.

322
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:09,880
Monsters who beat up innocent
girls are not welcome here.

323
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,960
I swear this wasn't me!

324
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:14,100
I promised you! Shut up!

325
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:15,500
Get out of here!

326
00:23:17,420 --> 00:23:18,250
Go!

327
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,777
Haven't you done enough?

328
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:21,897
Don't ever show your face here again!

329
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:22,810
Shut up!

330
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:23,850
Go on, leave!

331
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:27,077
Please, I wouldn't...

332
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:28,240
I couldn't...

333
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:35,100
This isn't happening.

334
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:38,460
I would never lay a hand on a lady.

335
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,520
Hey, German boy!

336
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:48,140
Found you!

337
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:52,500
What you doing over here?

338
00:23:52,820 --> 00:23:56,114
Hate to break it to you, but
the pleasure hall's closed.

339
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:57,270
No way.

340
00:23:57,353 --> 00:23:59,281
That's the last thing I would do.

341
00:23:59,660 --> 00:24:01,680
I could never hurt a woman.

342
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:03,190
Could I?

343
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:09,177
they beat a woman unconscious everything

344
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:11,907
you guys represent goes
against my principles

345
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:19,000
you're telling me i'm gonna end up like
them yeah my body isn't tingling anymore

346
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:23,357
maybe it already happened
i was caught up in my

347
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:26,322
thoughts when i ran into
that girl in the hallway

348
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:32,520
it took me a second to notice her and
then she went flying and she was bleeding

349
00:24:33,620 --> 00:24:35,920
She looked at me with fear in her eyes.

350
00:24:38,220 --> 00:24:39,050
Damn it.

351
00:24:41,740 --> 00:24:42,660
Hey, Luffy.

352
00:24:44,420 --> 00:24:46,891
What kind of man do you want on your crew?

353
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:52,560
An unreliable dreamer like me,
who's afraid of his own power,

354
00:24:52,940 --> 00:24:55,469
who's helpless every
time he faces a woman?

355
00:24:56,860 --> 00:24:59,337
Or a warrior of science who can beat up a

356
00:24:59,420 --> 00:25:01,357
monster like this
without a second thought,

357
00:25:01,440 --> 00:25:05,840
who has a heart of ice and a
will of steel that never fails.

358
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:11,576
Which would be more useful
to the King of the Pirates?

359
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:16,480
I need you on my crew, Saadji!

360
00:25:16,820 --> 00:25:17,900
Without you!

361
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:24,800
I don't know what'll happen
from here on out, but...

362
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:27,157
Is that the German suit?

363
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:28,534
Are you gonna wear it?

364
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:31,220
I know what I have to do.

365
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:38,080
When I put this suit on, it awakened a power
that's been inside me since I was born.

366
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:41,100
I can't do anything to change that.

367
00:25:41,620 --> 00:25:43,780
Sounds like you finally get it.

368
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:46,200
Now, suit up, Jermaboy!

369
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:50,520
But what I can do is put
an end to all of this.

370
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,920
I need you on my crew, Sanji!

371
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:03,480
Without you!

372
00:26:03,860 --> 00:26:05,060
Without you!

373
00:26:05,500 --> 00:26:08,200
I'll never be king of the pirates!

374
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,560
It's over.

375
00:26:14,540 --> 00:26:16,540
I'm choosing my own fate.

376
00:26:17,840 --> 00:26:19,437
What the hell are you doing?

377
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:21,600
I SAID PUT IT ON, NOT DESTROY IT!

378
00:26:25,620 --> 00:26:26,800
Goodbye, Jeremiah.

379
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:31,660
Goodbye, women's back.

380
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:36,660
I'm gonna finish this
fight, on my own terms.

381
00:26:52,460 --> 00:26:53,290
Collect

382
00:26:53,660 --> 00:26:54,680
What the hell?

383
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:56,626
So when do I have this thing?

384
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:02,200
Who's calling me at a time like this?

385
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:03,820
I'm busy!

386
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:08,758
I was afraid you might be
dying in a ditch somewhere.

387
00:27:08,980 --> 00:27:12,039
So I snuck that snail on
you as a safety precaution.

388
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:13,760
I'm not dying, you idiot!

389
00:27:15,700 --> 00:27:17,171
Could you leave me alone?

390
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:19,840
Listen, this won't take long.

391
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:26,180
I know we got this.

392
00:27:26,420 --> 00:27:29,185
We're beating the beast
pirates no matter what.

393
00:27:35,540 --> 00:27:36,960
Yeah, of course we are!

394
00:27:37,660 --> 00:27:38,960
But after the battle,

395
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:43,633
there's a chance I might not
be in my right mind anymore.

396
00:27:49,180 --> 00:27:52,200
If that happens, then kill me. What?

397
00:28:08,600 --> 00:28:09,700
You still there?

398
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:14,620
Yeah, I got it.

399
00:28:15,560 --> 00:28:16,640
No problem.

400
00:28:17,100 --> 00:28:19,480
I'll kill you, just like you asked.

401
00:28:20,780 --> 00:28:25,604
I don't get what your problem is, but at
least I got something to look forward to.

402
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:29,520
So until then,

403
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:33,440
don't you dare die on me.

404
00:28:34,460 --> 00:28:36,140
I appreciate it.

405
00:28:36,660 --> 00:28:37,490
Galick.

406
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:44,360
Hey, where'd you go?

407
00:28:44,680 --> 00:28:46,209
You got invisibility tech?

408
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:47,590
What?

409
00:28:47,673 --> 00:28:48,741
Bet Daddy gave you that too, huh?

410
00:28:50,860 --> 00:28:53,380
I don't need you adding fuel to the fire!

411
00:28:58,480 --> 00:29:00,820
Cause I'm already burning up!

412
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:07,220
I'm sending you straight to hell!

413
00:29:12,700 --> 00:29:13,880
Hell's memories!
